From c41b69fe9a3a6cdd9efe7697efa69a40eba17c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:39:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: adapt M4 to the desktop kernel

Use the Linux 7.1 Io and ARef interfaces and release revocable MMIO guards before allocations, sleeps, and firmware calls. Reacquire guards around register access.

Integrate the early crash-buffer handshake with the existing boot-AP ownership path, retaining its wait before the optional early return. Keep the saved helper placement and documentation, and omit the unused IoSysMap read extension.

Assisted-By: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra)
Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
